From: Fountain5405 <Fountain5405@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:15:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/27] tests: pool and block paths reject the same
 transactions

tx_batch_gates runs the same transactions through the pool path (one
at a time) and the block path (ver_non_input_consensus over a
pool_supplement), in batches of 1 to 33, below and above the sizes
where the block path batches its key-image domain checks (8) and splits
its sum checks (16). A key image outside the prime-order subgroup, a
bad BP+ proof and a broken balance are rejected by both, with the same
flags. A sweep puts one defective transaction at listed positions, and
several in different sub-batches; each sinks the whole block.

It also checks that make_input_verification_id binds the transaction,
the tree root and the layer count, and pins the output-type rules of
check_output_types at hf16 and at hf17 (HF_VERSION_CARROT), so that a
change to the hf17 rule shows up before that fork activates.

Written by the second reviewer; adopted here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
